import json
I=[
("Recall Check Before Sign-Up","Trust","Let a visitor type a brand and model (or snap a label) and instantly see if it has an open recall, free. It proves the Recall Tracking promise on the first screen and is the kind of hook people share.","Recall Tracking is one line on the home page","'Check Your Water Heater for Recalls' tool, then 'Track All My Equipment' button",None),
("Snap a Label, Auto-Fill the Model and Serial","Photos","On the photo step, read the brand, model and serial from the label photo and show them back for a quick confirm. Fewer typing steps, and the quote gets exact equipment data.","Photo cards just collect pictures","Photo, then 'Rheem XG50T, Serial 0423...' with Looks Right / Fix It","c-photos.jpg"),
("Add Visits to My Calendar","After Sign-Up","On the confirmation screen, offer an .ics download (or Google Calendar link) for the first visit and the seasonal schedule. Members stop forgetting visits and no-shows drop.","Confirmation shows a summary only","'Add My Visit Schedule to Calendar' button with 4 seasonal events",None),
("Fix the Silver vs Platinum Mismatch","Pricing","The video's closing card shows $99 Silver and $219 Gold, but the app offers Gold and Platinum at thousands a year. Pick one lineup (the research suggests Silver, Gold, Platinum) and make the video and app match.","Video: $99 Silver, $219 Gold. App: Gold $2,780+, Platinum","One lineup everywhere, same names and prices",None),
("Add a Silver Entry Tier","Pricing","The pricing research shows Gold at $2,600+ is a big first purchase; a 2-visit Silver at about $900 to $1,300 gets you into the house and the visit report sells the upgrade.","Gold or Platinum only","Silver, Gold (Most Popular), Platinum cards","c-tier.jpg"),
("Show Monthly Price First","Pricing","Lead with 'About $232 a month' and put the yearly total underneath, and let Gold be paid monthly or quarterly too. Big annual numbers scare people off at the moment they decide.","$2,780 / year, paid annually up front","$232 / month, billed monthly (or $2,780 a year)","c-tier.jpg"),
("Write Clear Cancellation Terms","Legal","The agreement says cancellation and refund terms are to be determined. State them plainly (for example, cancel anytime before the next visit, prorated refund) and show a one-line version next to the price.","'Cancellation and refund terms are to be determined.'","'Cancel anytime. Unused visits refunded.' under each price","c-legal.jpg"),
("Finalize the Agreement and Waiver","Legal","Both are marked Draft, Pending Legal Review. Get them reviewed and swap in final text before taking real sign-ups, since a draft label right before signing kills trust.","Two DRAFT boxes and two signatures","One final agreement, one signature, a summary of key terms","c-legal.jpg"),
("Turn On Real Payments","Checkout","The payment fields are disabled with a 'Demo' note, so nobody can actually buy. Wire up Stripe Checkout (or a 'Reserve Now, Pay at First Visit' option) so the funnel converts.","Disabled card fields, 'Complete Sign Up (Demo)'","Stripe Checkout or 'Reserve My Spot, Pay After First Visit'","c-pay.jpg"),
("Collect a Waitlist for Out-of-Area ZIPs","Funnel","A ZIP like 90210 only gets a warning and then a metro Detroit estimate that means nothing. Instead say 'We are not there yet' and capture an email so you know where demand is.","Warning, then 'tap Next again to continue'","'Not in your area yet. Want a heads-up when we are?' + email","c-zip.jpg"),
("Hide the Prototype Badge","Trust","The header says 'Prototype, Draft Pricing' on every screen. For real homeowners, drop it and keep the 'estimate' wording near the price instead.","'PROTOTYPE, DRAFT PRICING' tag in the header","Clean header with logo and a Call or Text button","c-header.jpg"),
("Don't Auto-Open the Video","Speed","The explainer opens in a full-screen modal on first visit and downloads a 4 MB video before people see anything. Show the page first, with a poster card that plays the video on tap.","Modal video covers the home page","Hero with a small 'Watch 60s Video' poster thumbnail","c-video.jpg"),
("Add Real Trust Signals","Trust","Show license and insurance numbers, a named local owner, reviews or a 'Founding Member' count, and a satisfaction guarantee near the Get Started button. Today the claims have no proof.","'Licensed & Insured Techs' with no detail","License #, insurer, '4.9 stars from 31 neighbors', guarantee badge","c-hero.jpg"),
("Add a Call or Text Us Button","Trust","There is no phone number or contact anywhere. A sticky Text Us button gives nervous buyers a human and catches leads who won't fill a form.","No contact option","'Questions? Text Us' in the header and on the price screen","c-header.jpg"),
("Explain Unsure Answers on the Price","Funnel","After 8 Unsure answers the price quietly assumes a typical home. Show which answers were guessed with a one-tap fix, so the price feels honest rather than random.","'You answered Unsure 8 times'","List: 'Furnaces: guessed 1, Fix' for each Unsure","c-unsure.jpg"),
("Show a Price Range While Answering","Funnel","Show a small running estimate (for example $2,400 to $3,200) that narrows as they answer. It rewards each answer and avoids sticker shock at the end.","Price appears only at Step 3","Sticky 'Your estimate so far: $2.4k to $3.2k' bar",None),
("Shorter Path: Skip Straight to a Price","Funnel","Offer 'Just Give Me a Ballpark' after the ZIP and home size, filling the rest with typical values. Impatient visitors still see a number and can refine later.","7 questions before any price","ZIP + size, then 'See Ballpark' or 'Refine My Price'",None),
("Save Progress and Email the Quote","Funnel","Let people email themselves the estimate or get a resume link. Most homeowners decide with a spouse, so they need to come back later.","Progress only in this browser","'Email Me This Quote' button on the price screen",None),
("Spell Out What a Visit Looks Like","Copy","Add a simple timeline: 'Fall visit: furnace tune-up, gutter clean, smoke and CO test, 90 minutes'. People buy what they can picture.","Long bullet lists per tier","4 season cards with what happens and how long",None),
("Compare Against Booking It Yourself","Pricing","Show 'What this costs a la carte in metro Detroit' next to the membership price, using the research numbers. It frames the membership as savings, but only if the numbers truly hold up.","Price with no reference point","'Booked separately: about $3,400. With Gold: $2,780.'",None),
("Make the Signature Step Lighter","Checkout","Two separate draw-or-type signatures plus two checkboxes is a lot on a phone. Use one combined 'I agree to the Agreement and Waiver' checkbox with a typed name.","2 checkboxes, 2 signature pads","1 checkbox + typed full name",None),
("Label Every Form Field for Screen Readers","Accessibility","Five inputs on the sign-up step (typed signatures and card fields) have no linked label. Add proper labels and error announcements so screen readers and autofill work.","5 inputs with no label","All inputs labelled, autocomplete set (name, tel, email, street-address)",None),
("Add to Home Screen After Sign-Up","After Sign-Up","After joining, offer a small dismissible 'Keep Smart Upkeep on your phone' card, so members can see their schedule and reports like an app.","Nothing after confirmation","Dismissible install card with Add / Not Now",None),
("Offline Shutoffs and Emergency Info for Members","After Sign-Up","After the first visit, give members a page with photos of their own water, gas and electric shutoffs that works offline. It is useful on the worst day and makes the membership sticky.","Shutoff valves checked, not recorded for the owner","'My Shutoffs' page with photos and steps, works offline",None),
("A Sample Visit Report","Trust","Link a sample written report (photos, findings, next steps) from the price screen. It shows the value of 'Written report after every visit' better than a bullet.","'Written report after every visit' bullet","'See a Sample Report' link opens a 1-page example",None),
("Seasonal Reminders by Text","After Sign-Up","Text members a day before each visit and a short tip each season (for example 'Change your furnace filter'). It keeps the brand top of mind and cuts no-shows.","No reminders","Opt-in SMS checkbox at sign-up",None),
("Referral Credit","Growth","Give a credit (for example one free month) for each neighbor who joins. Home services spread by word of mouth in a neighborhood.","No referral option","'Share With a Neighbor, Both Get a Month Free' on confirmation","c-foot.jpg"),
]
out=[{"id":f"2026-10-12-{n+1}","title":t,"cat":c,"what":w,"before":b,"after":a,"img":("img/"+i if i else None)} for n,(t,c,w,b,a,i) in enumerate(I)]
json.dump(out,open("ideas.json","w"),indent=1)
md=["# Smart Upkeep Improvement Ideas (2026-10-12)","","Swipe app: https://webermanapps.github.io/smart-upkeep-ideas/","",f"{len(out)} suggestions from a homeowner walkthrough of https://webermanapps.github.io/smart-upkeep/, the 48322 pricing research, Max's Daily Ideas votes and the known gaps. Screenshot crops live in the swipe app repo under img/.",""]
for n,x in enumerate(out):
    md+= [f"## {n+1}. {x['title']}",f"*{x['cat']}*","",x['what'],"",f"- **Before:** {x['before']}",f"- **After:** {x['after']}"]+([f"- Screenshot: {x['img']}"] if x['img'] else [])+[""]
open("/workspace/smartkeep/ideas/2026-10-12.md","w").write("\n".join(md));print(len(out))
